#. Tag: title
#: docked_windows.docbook:1
#, no-c-format
msgid "Docked windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kappname; interface is composed of a number of smaller docked windows. "
"Manipulating these windows can be difficult at first. To focus a particular "
"window in the &kappname; interface, simply click within it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each docked window has a small grip bar along the top. It contains a dock/"
"undock button resembling an arrow at its right end and a close button "
"resembling the letter X. It looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: docked_windows.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Grip bar of a docked window</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: docked_windows.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Grip bar of a docked window</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking the close button on a docked window will remove it from the "
"interface. To bring it back, select its name in the <guimenu>Window</"
"guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "To resize docked windows, drag the border between the windows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To re-arrange the docked windows, drag a window by its grip bar over to the "
"desired position. While dragging, a small box outline will appear to "
"indicate the position the window will take when you end the drag."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you wish to stack two windows and use tabs to choose between them, drag "
"the window to the very center of the other window with which you wish to "
"stack."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To undock a window, either click the dock/undock button in its top right "
"corner, or double-click on the window's grip bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Double-clicking again or clicking on the dock/undock button, should return "
"the window to its original position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also dock an undocked window by dragging its grip bar back to a "
"point within the general interface, just as if you were rearranging an "
"already docked window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The file view window cannot be undocked or moved, but by moving other "
"windows around, it can itself be shifted about."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docked_windows.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While dragging a window, press the <keycap>Escape</keycap> key to cancel the "
"operation. To reset the docked windows to the default &kappname; layout, use "
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Window</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Reset</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice>."
msgstr ""
